{"agent_id":"pp3g-jlse-validation-task-evidence-only-not-a-system-to-ship","agent_seq":29,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T03:03:21.685190608Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"931ad307-386e-4096-8e00-0d9a4388216f","comment_uuid":"a550b69a-7b6f-4ac3-9cc2-e6b28d9a38a6","author":"pp3g-jlse-validation-task-evidence-only-not-a-system-to-ship","content":"[REVIEWER DIVERGENCE - for orchestrator adjudication] On re-reading this issue after posting, I see an earlier handoff comment (02:55) from another agent that reviewed the same deliverable and concluded 'deliverable PASS, claims corroborated'. My result (02:59) concludes CHANGES REQUESTED. Flagging rather than silently reconciling, per AGENTS.md on constructive disagreement.\n\nIndependence note: my analysis was complete before I saw that comment. Issue #199 carried no comments when I loaded it at 02:41; I worked only from the artifacts and the installed venv.\n\nThe two reviews do not actually contradict on facts - they differ on what was checked. Points of agreement: all five test verdicts hold; the timings the report states are correctly derived from the logs; every source citation is exact; the list_changed source read replicates including _vendor. We independently verified the same figures (2807 / 2614 / 10 / 2639 / 14-17-7 / 1587 / 2665 / 2786 / 1453) and got identical results.\n\nMy CHANGES REQUESTED rests on four things that follow from asking a different question - not 'do the stated numbers reconcile' but 'are the stated numbers the right summary of the corpus':\n1. The report quotes cold-start from one sample; the logs contain three for the identical path (2155 / 2639 / 2761). Both reviews confirmed 2639 is correctly derived - it is just not the whole evidence base, and the observed ceiling is 2761.\n2. Backend init is characterised as 1.1-1.3s while two of the four logged init_ms values (1345.0, 1573.6) sit outside that band.\n3. The conclusion never names the stdio-only scope, while section 6 recommends a longer-lived transport that was never tested.\n4. The 'capabilities omit tools/list_changed' claim is contradicted by mcp/server/lowlevel/server.py:605-606, which constructs ToolsCapability(list_changed=False) whenever a tools/list handler is registered. The other review verified NotificationOptions tools_changed=False - which is correct and is the input to that line - but the output is an advertised listChanged:false, not an omission.\n\nNone of these change a PASS/FAIL verdict. All four are accuracy/scope defects in an artifact whose stated purpose is evidence, which is why I graded them blocking rather than advisory. The orchestrator may reasonably weigh them as non-blocking; the underlying facts are not in dispute.\n\nAlso noting the other reviewer was blocked from a live re-run and recommended one. I did not attempt a re-run either - my verification was entirely static (log arithmetic plus source inspection of the installed packages), so neither review independently re-executed the harness. That gap stands.","created_at":"2026-08-06T03:03:21.677296370Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:dqJJxDfhYp2s0PbFtktYlMdwFUCtHuPimgtdoZJSG+g","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgi3Y7k6zLHSnYcebt0U8E4gaHZmVqfalyr69g11qwxm8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABATwVKhqXrCp/gjz5WV4iPlHB/1RI8Gn0hnDLg2RKhyUPkLVLKo9mTHpbrbnGXyQy12qzm3I69pGyrrH1eJCZkBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:dqJJxDfhYp2s0PbFtktYlMdwFUCtHuPimgtdoZJSG+g","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgi3Y7k6zLHSnYcebt0U8E4gaHZmVqfalyr69g11qwxm8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCFT5/cNDiqx+SJymbykRtCwfsgOXtpEral6j2R9ju8teVDFWVGVhwT2x85aFpH2Vv8ESlH0QRFnt4sj52QPKQQ="}
